      <Docs>
        <summary>
          <para>Use the default sync source (default). If media has video, the sync renders to a surface that directly renders to a display, and tolerance is non zero (e.g. not less than 0.001) vsync source is used for clock source. Otherwise, if media has audio, audio track is used. Finally, if media has no audio, system clock is used.</para>
          <para><format type="text/html"><a href="https://developer.android.com/reference/android/media/SyncParams#SYNC_SOURCE_DEFAULT" title="Reference documentation">Android reference for <code>android.media.SyncParams.SYNC_SOURCE_DEFAULT</code>.</a></format></para>
